### EFAR API - Xero Foundation, OCR & AP Processing (Kwan Hua implementation)
### Requires the "REST Client" VS Code extension (humao.rest-client).
###
### Prerequisites:
### 1. Backend running locally: cd backend && node src/index.js  (default PORT=3000)
### 2. Demo users seeded:        node src/scripts/seed-users.js
###    (all demo accounts share the password "Efar@2026")
### 3. Optional but recommended: node src/scripts/seed-xero.js
###    seeds an active (simulated) Xero connection so approve/sync/retry requests
###    below don't 503 with XERO_NOT_CONNECTED. XERO_SIMULATION defaults to "true"
###    (see backend/.env.example), so Xero pushes are faked - no real Xero account
###    is required to exercise the happy paths.
### 4. The upload endpoint's happy path (section 5) genuinely calls Gemini + Cloudinary -
###    it needs a real GEMINI_API_KEY and Cloudinary credentials in backend/.env.
###    Without them it will 502 (CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_FAILED / OCR_EXTRACTION_FAILED) -
###    that's expected, not a bug in this file.
###
### The four login requests below are run once each; their response tokens are
### captured into variables and reused automatically by every request below via
### {{loginX.response.body.$.data.token}} - no need to copy/paste tokens manually.
###
### A few endpoints have no request body at all (GET /status, GET /connect,
### DELETE /disconnect, POST /approve, POST /reextract, POST /retry), so a literal
### "missing/invalid field -> 400" test doesn't apply to them. Those sections
### substitute the closest real negative-path test that endpoint actually has,
### and say so explicitly in the comment.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api
@contentType = application/json

### ============================================================
### AUTH - one token per role used across this file
### managing_director: Xero connect/disconnect (UC-01)
### ap_specialist:      vendor invoices + line items (UC-03..07)
### ar_specialist:       shared sync-log panel (UC-08)
### quotations_specialist: has NO permission anywhere below - used for 403 checks
### ============================================================

# @name loginMd
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "doris@efar.com.sg",
  "password": "Efar@2026"
}

###

@mdToken = {{loginMd.response.body.$.data.token}}

# @name loginAp
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "chloe@efar.com.sg",
  "password": "Efar@2026"
}

###

@apToken = {{loginAp.response.body.$.data.token}}

# @name loginAr
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "sarah@efar.com.sg",
  "password": "Efar@2026"
}

###

@arToken = {{loginAr.response.body.$.data.token}}

# @name loginWrongRole
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "camilla@efar.com.sg",
  "password": "Efar@2026"
}

###

@wrongRoleToken = {{loginWrongRole.response.body.$.data.token}}


### ============================================================
### Fill these in as you go - copy real ids from the responses above/below.
### ============================================================
@vendorInvoiceId = 1
@vendorInvoiceItemId = 1
@syncLogId = 1


### ============================================================
### 1. GET /api/xero/status  (UC-01)
### ============================================================

### Happy path: authenticated as ar_specialist (also allowed: ap_specialist, managing_director)
### Expect: 200 OK, { is_connected, xero_org_name, xero_tenant_id, connected_at, token_expiry }
GET {{baseUrl}}/xero/status
Authorization: Bearer {{arToken}}

###

### No fields to validate on a bodyless GET - substituting the endpoint's real
### role-check negative path instead (quotations_specialist is not in the allowed list)
### Expect: 403 FORBIDDEN
GET {{baseUrl}}/xero/status
Authorization: Bearer {{wrongRoleToken}}

###

### No auth: Authorization header omitted entirely
### Expect: 401 UNAUTHORIZED ("Missing or invalid token.")
GET {{baseUrl}}/xero/status


### ============================================================
### 2. GET /api/xero/connect  (UC-01 step 3, managing_director only)
### ============================================================

### Happy path: valid managing_director token, Xero client_id/redirect_uri configured
### Expect: 200 OK, { auth_url } pointing at login.xero.com with client_id/scope/state
GET {{baseUrl}}/xero/connect
Authorization: Bearer {{mdToken}}

###

### No fields to validate on a bodyless GET - substituting the endpoint's real
### role-check negative path (only managing_director may initiate the OAuth2 flow)
### Expect: 403 FORBIDDEN
GET {{baseUrl}}/xero/connect
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}

###

### No auth: Authorization header omitted entirely
### Expect: 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{baseUrl}}/xero/connect


### ============================================================
### 3. GET /api/xero/callback  (UC-01 steps 5-7, no auth - called by Xero's redirect)
### ============================================================
### This endpoint always responds with a 302 redirect back to the frontend, never JSON,
### so it doesn't fit the happy/400/401 pattern used elsewhere in this file:
###   - There is no "no auth" case - this route intentionally has none (CSRF is handled
###     via the single-use `state` param instead of a JWT).
###   - Its "invalid input" cases are redirects with an ?error=... query flag, not a 400.
### `state` must be a real value freshly issued by request #2 above (it's single-use and
### server-side), so copy it out of that response's `auth_url` query string before running
### the happy-path request below. `code` can be any non-empty string - XERO_SIMULATION=true
### (the default) short-circuits the real Xero token exchange.

@xeroState = paste-the-state-value-from-the-connect-response-here

### Happy path: real single-use state + a placeholder code (simulation mode)
### Expect: 302 redirect to {FRONTEND_URL}/settings/xero?connected=true
GET {{baseUrl}}/xero/callback?code=sim-code-123&state={{xeroState}}

###

### Xero denied permission: `error` query param present
### Expect: 302 redirect to .../settings/xero?error=access_denied
GET {{baseUrl}}/xero/callback?error=access_denied&state={{xeroState}}

###

### Invalid/reused state (CSRF check fails, or you re-run this after using it once already)
### Expect: 302 redirect to .../settings/xero?error=invalid_state
GET {{baseUrl}}/xero/callback?code=sim-code-123&state=not-a-real-state


### ============================================================
### 4. DELETE /api/xero/disconnect  (UC-01, managing_director only)
### ============================================================

### Happy path: valid managing_director token, an active connection exists
### (run request #3's happy path first, or node src/scripts/seed-xero.js)
### Expect: 200 OK, { message: "Xero disconnected successfully." }
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/xero/disconnect
Authorization: Bearer {{mdToken}}

###

### No fields to validate on a bodyless DELETE - substituting the endpoint's real
### "nothing to disconnect" negative path: run this a second time right after the one above
### Expect: 404 NOT_CONNECTED
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/xero/disconnect
Authorization: Bearer {{mdToken}}

###

### No auth: Authorization header omitted entirely
### Expect: 401 UNAUTHORIZED
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/xero/disconnect


### ============================================================
### 5. POST /api/vendor-invoices  (UC-03/04/05, ap_specialist only, multipart/form-data)
### ============================================================

### Happy path: valid PDF, default 1% rebate (requires real GEMINI_API_KEY + Cloudinary
### credentials in backend/.env - see prerequisite #4 at the top of this file)
### Expect: 201 Created, vendor_invoices row with status "pending_review",
### extracted fields + rebate_amount/verified_total populated
POST {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----efar-boundary

------efar-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="CMD-2026-01187.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./src/scripts/fixtures/CMD-2026-01187.pdf
------efar-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="rebate_percentage"

1.00
------efar-boundary--

###

### Invalid input: wrong file type (PDF-only endpoint, this sends nothing recognisable as one)
### Expect: 400 INVALID_FILE_TYPE ("Only PDF files are accepted...")
POST {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----efar-boundary

------efar-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="not-an-invoice.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

This is not a PDF.
------efar-boundary--

###

### No auth: Authorization header omitted entirely
### Expect: 401 UNAUTHORIZED
POST {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----efar-boundary

------efar-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="CMD-2026-01187.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./src/scripts/fixtures/CMD-2026-01187.pdf
------efar-boundary--


### ============================================================
### 6. GET /api/vendor-invoices  (UC-06/07, ap_specialist + managing_director)
### ============================================================

### Happy path: default pagination, no filters
### Expect: 200 OK, { data: [...], pagination: { page: 1, limit: 20, ... } }
GET {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}

###

### Invalid input: date_from is after date_to
### Expect: 400 INVALID_DATE_RANGE
GET {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices?date_from=2026-06-30&date_to=2026-06-01
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}

###

### No auth: Authorization header omitted entirely
### Expect: 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices


### ============================================================
### 7. GET /api/vendor-invoices/:id  (UC-06, ap_specialist + managing_director)
### ============================================================

### Happy path: an id that exists (update @vendorInvoiceId above if needed)
### Expect: 200 OK, full detail incl. items[]
GET {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices/{{vendorInvoiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}

###

### No fields to validate on a bodyless GET - substituting the closest real negative
### path: an id that doesn't exist
### Expect: 404 NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}

###

### No auth: Authorization header omitted entirely
### Expect: 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices/{{vendorInvoiceId}}


### ============================================================
### 8. PATCH /api/vendor-invoices/:id  (UC-06, ap_specialist only)
### ============================================================

### Happy path: correct a header field on a pending_review invoice
### Expect: 200 OK, field updated, rebate recalculated if extracted_total changed
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices/{{vendorInvoiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "vendor_name": "Esso Petroleum Singapore Pte Ltd",
  "extracted_total": 1840.00
}

###

### Invalid input: extracted_total is not a positive number
### Expect: 400 INVALID_TOTAL
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices/{{vendorInvoiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "extracted_total": -50
}

###

### No auth: Authorization header omitted entirely
### Expect: 401 UNAUTHORIZED
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices/{{vendorInvoiceId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "vendor_name": "Should not be allowed"
}


### ============================================================
### 9. POST /api/vendor-invoices/:id/approve  (UC-06/07, ap_specialist only)
### ============================================================

### Happy path: invoice is pending_review with extracted_total set, Xero connected
### Expect: 200 OK, status "synced_to_xero" (or "failed" if the simulated push fails)
POST {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices/{{vendorInvoiceId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}

###

### No fields to validate on a bodyless POST - substituting the endpoint's real
### "not enough data to approve" negative path: extracted_total is not set
### Expect: 409 MISSING_TOTAL
POST {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices/{{vendorInvoiceId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}

###

### No auth: Authorization header omitted entirely
### Expect: 401 UNAUTHORIZED
POST {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices/{{vendorInvoiceId}}/approve


### ============================================================
### 10. POST /api/vendor-invoices/:id/reject  (UC-06, ap_specialist only)
### ============================================================

### Happy path: valid rejection_reason on a pending_review invoice
### Expect: 200 OK, status "rejected", reason stored
POST {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices/{{vendorInvoiceId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "rejection_reason": "Invoice does not belong to EFAR - vendor address does not match our accounts."
}

###

### Invalid input: rejection_reason missing
### Expect: 400 MISSING_REASON
POST {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices/{{vendorInvoiceId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{}

###

### No auth: Authorization header omitted entirely
### Expect: 401 UNAUTHORIZED
POST {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices/{{vendorInvoiceId}}/reject
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "rejection_reason": "Should not be allowed without a token."
}


### ============================================================
### 11. POST /api/vendor-invoices/:id/reextract  (UC-04, ap_specialist only)
### ============================================================

### Happy path: invoice is pending_review or extraction_failed
### Expect: 200 OK, new extraction replaces the previous fields + line items
POST {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices/{{vendorInvoiceId}}/reextract
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}

###

### No fields to validate on a bodyless POST - substituting the endpoint's real
### status-guard negative path: re-run this against an invoice already approved/synced/rejected
### Expect: 409 INVALID_STATUS
POST {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices/{{vendorInvoiceId}}/reextract
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}

###

### No auth: Authorization header omitted entirely
### Expect: 401 UNAUTHORIZED
POST {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices/{{vendorInvoiceId}}/reextract


### ============================================================
### 12. PATCH /api/vendor-invoice-items/:id  (UC-06, ap_specialist only)
### ============================================================

### Happy path: correct a line item's amount on an editable parent invoice
### Expect: 200 OK, item updated, parent_invoice totals recomputed from all items
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoice-items/{{vendorInvoiceItemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "amount": 1740.00
}

###

### Invalid input: amount is not a positive number
### Expect: 400 INVALID_AMOUNT
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoice-items/{{vendorInvoiceItemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "amount": 0
}

###

### No auth: Authorization header omitted entirely
### Expect: 401 UNAUTHORIZED
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoice-items/{{vendorInvoiceItemId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "amount": 1740.00
}


### ============================================================
### 13. GET /api/xero/sync-logs  (UC-08, ap_specialist + ar_specialist + managing_director)
### ============================================================

### Happy path: default pagination, no filters
### Expect: 200 OK, { data: [...], pagination, xero_connected }
GET {{baseUrl}}/xero/sync-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{arToken}}

###

### Invalid input: status is not one of pending/success/failed
### Expect: 400 VALIDATION_ERROR ("Invalid status filter")
GET {{baseUrl}}/xero/sync-logs?status=bogus
Authorization: Bearer {{arToken}}

###

### No auth: Authorization header omitted entirely
### Expect: 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{baseUrl}}/xero/sync-logs


### ============================================================
### 14. POST /api/xero/sync-logs/:id/retry  (UC-08, ap_specialist + ar_specialist)
### ============================================================

### Happy path: log status is "failed", attempt_count < 3, Xero connected
### Expect: 200 OK, status "success" (or "failed" again if the simulated push still fails)
POST {{baseUrl}}/xero/sync-logs/{{syncLogId}}/retry
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}

###

### No fields to validate on a bodyless POST - substituting the endpoint's real
### status-guard negative path: retry a log that is not currently "failed"
### Expect: 409 NOT_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/xero/sync-logs/{{syncLogId}}/retry
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}

###

### No auth: Authorization header omitted entirely
### Expect: 401 UNAUTHORIZED
POST {{baseUrl}}/xero/sync-logs/{{syncLogId}}/retry


### ============================================================
### BONUS: a real inconsistency worth knowing about
### ============================================================

### uploadVendorInvoice validates rebate_percentage with its OWN inline Yup schema
### (0-100), separately from the shared `validate()` middleware used everywhere else
### in this file. Its catch block returns a Yup ValidationError as 422, not 400 -
### the only endpoint in this feature area that does. Every other "invalid input"
### case above is a genuine 400.
### Expect: 422 VALIDATION_ERROR (not 400 - flagging this as a real inconsistency)
POST {{baseUrl}}/vendor-invoices
Authorization: Bearer {{apToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----efar-boundary

------efar-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="CMD-2026-01187.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./src/scripts/fixtures/CMD-2026-01187.pdf
------efar-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="rebate_percentage"

150

------efar-boundary--
